// @corpus: platform
// @id: PLATFORM-clock
// @category: platform — time
// @charter: §7.5, §14 M5
// @milestone: E2C
//
// Reading the clock is an EFFECT, which is what makes a wall-clock read inside
// a shared deterministic materialization detectable (corpus R-017) rather than
// a code-review question.

module clock

// **A point in time** (ADR-0180, charter §15.1's `generated_at`): the
// milliseconds since 1970-01-01T00:00Z, as a wall clock reads them. One
// `Int`, so two order and subtract; no invariant, since an instant before
// 1970 is still one.
opaque type Instant = Int

fn now() -> Int !{ clock.read } { 0 }

// `clock.wall` and `clock.read` are different effects because they break
// different things. A monotonic read gives a duration; a WALL read gives a
// value that depends on when the code ran, so an artifact generated once and
// served many times is no longer a function of its inputs (corpus R-016,
// R-017). The family alone would not tell them apart.
fn now_wall() -> Int !{ clock.wall } { 0 }

fn today() -> String !{ clock.wall } { "" }
